; Shell-startup: every shell that NewShell starts reads this before it
; takes its first line from the console, and so does one `s3> newshell`
; starts.

Prompt "%N.%S> "

; Clear: the cursor to the top left, and everything from there erased.
; An alias is the shell's own, so S:Startup-Sequence makes it too.
Alias Clear "Echo NOLINE *"*E[0;0H*E[J*""
